# tools/ales_bell_witness.rish — a parametric bell (peaking EQ): turn the middle band, hold the edges (ALES48).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES48.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-170143_fill-ales48-lotus-parametric-bell.md
# Stands on: lotus/tone.rye (ALES40 — low_pass, high_pass, precheck), lotus/notch.rye (ALES47 — the zero-gain equality target),
# lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip and saturate); residual shape from lotus/stack.rye (ALES42).
#
# lotus/bell.rye keeps the low and high edges at unity and scales the mid band — the exact residual M = x − L − H — by a gain,
# summed and clamped once. The selftest proves: silence stays silence; unity gain is the identity (low + high + M = x); zero gain
# IS ALES47's band-reject byte-for-byte (proven against notch.notch); a constant settles to itself at any gain (the mid is zero at
# direct current, so the edges never move); a heavy boost saturates rather than wraps; an illegal cutoff on either edge refuses
# BadCoeff, a zero gain denominator BadGain, an out-of-range span BadRange. Purely local — no network, no keys, no funds, no real
# device, no real sample rate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_bell_witness.rish

say "ales-bell: Language EN — ALES48 keeps ALES40's low and high edges at unity and scales the residual middle band by a gain, the parametric bell (peaking EQ) — the single most-reached-for tool in a mix: lift a vocal's presence, tame a boxy room mode, dig out a kick's thump."
say "ales-bell: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: unity gain reconstructs the input byte-for-byte, zero gain is exactly the band-reject, and a constant settles to itself at any gain because the middle is zero at direct current — the bell turns only what lies between the cutoffs."
say "ales-bell: Lens TAME — bounded Clip, u32 span, i16 samples, two scratch edges and the residual middle scaled and summed in i64 with a single clamp (ALES8's fader lesson); both cutoffs checked up front through tone.precheck, a zero gain denominator refuses BadGain; the bell adds no arithmetic on the audio path beyond the one gain; an out-of-range span refuses BadRange, each before a write; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no sample rate."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/bell"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/bell.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-bell: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/bell.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-bell: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-bell: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-bell' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-bell: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-bell line"

# The bell at zero gain IS the notch — prove ALES47's band-reject still stands by its own green, so the identity is honest.
let notch = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/notch.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/notch && lotus/bin/notch selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-notch' && echo yes"]
assert (trim notch.out) == "yes" else "ales-bell: the ALES47 band-reject witness regressed under the bell"

say "ales-bell: GREEN — a parametric bell turns the middle band and holds the edges by scaling the exact residual M = x − L − H, summed and clamped once; unity gain is the identity byte-for-byte, zero gain IS the band-reject (proven against notch.notch), a constant settles to itself at both a boost and a full cut (the mid is zero at direct current), and a heavy boost saturates to the rail rather than wrapping; an illegal cutoff refuses BadCoeff, a zero gain denominator BadGain, an out-of-range span BadRange, each leaving the clip untouched; the ALES47 band-reject selftest stays GREEN. With the low-pass, high-pass, shelf, stack, band-pass, band-reject, and now the parametric bell, the fixed-EQ family is whole — the next Lotus rung can sweep the bell's centre, give it a real hertz and a Q, or automate its gain under an envelope."
